# CODEOWNERS — [Project Name]
#
# Per _spine/code-review-agent/knowledge/03-sensitive-paths.md
# Required reviewers per file path. Branch protection enforces this.
#
# Format: <pattern> @user1 @user2 @team

# ============================================================
# Default — any senior dev can approve
# ============================================================
* @your-senior-dev-1 @your-senior-dev-2

# ============================================================
# Sensitive paths — require specific senior approval
# ============================================================

# Checkout customization (Shopify Plus only)
/checkout.liquid                                @your-senior-dev-2 @your-tech-lead

# Cart sections + snippets
/sections/**cart**                              @your-senior-dev-2 @your-tech-lead
/snippets/**cart**                              @your-senior-dev-2 @your-tech-lead
/assets/**cart**.js                             @your-senior-dev-2 @your-tech-lead

# Payment-related files
/snippets/**payment**                           @your-senior-dev-2 @your-tech-lead
**/*payment*                                    @your-senior-dev-2 @your-tech-lead

# Price calculations
/snippets/**price**                             @your-senior-dev-2 @your-tech-lead

# Customer accounts
/templates/customers/                           @your-senior-dev-2 @your-tech-lead

# Section schemas (impact across project)
/sections/*.liquid                              @your-tech-lead

# Theme settings
/config/settings_schema.json                    @your-tech-lead

# ============================================================
# Security-sensitive
# ============================================================
**/*auth*                                       @your-senior-dev-2 @your-tech-lead
**/*login*                                      @your-senior-dev-2 @your-tech-lead

# ============================================================
# Configuration
# ============================================================
/.env*                                          @your-tech-lead
/.github/                                       @your-tech-lead
/CODEOWNERS                                     @your-tech-lead
/.theme-check.yml                               @your-tech-lead

# ============================================================
# Documentation (less strict)
# ============================================================
*.md                                            @your-senior-dev-1 @your-senior-dev-2
/AGENCY-MASTER-DOC.md                           @your-tech-lead

# ============================================================
# Instructions for setting this up
# ============================================================
#
# 1. Replace placeholder usernames with actual GitHub usernames or teams:
#    @your-senior-dev-1 → @actual-username
#    @your-senior-dev-2 → @actual-username
#    @your-tech-lead → @actual-username
#
# 2. Copy this file to .github/CODEOWNERS in the project repo
#    (lowercase folder, ALL CAPS filename, no extension)
#
# 3. Enable branch protection for main + develop with required reviewers:
#    Repo Settings → Branches → Add rule
#      - Require approvals from Code Owners: ON
#      - Require approvals: 1 (or 2 for main)
#
# 4. Code Review Agent reads this file to identify sensitive paths
#    automatically and surfaces them in PR comments.
